.el .ds Aq '
.TH batten-capture-find 1  batten 
.SH NAME
batten\-capture\-find \- Resolve a stored tool response by the key it carries, with no handle to look up first
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBbatten capture find\fR [\fB\-\-key\-at\fR] [\fB\-\-raw\fR] [\fB\-J\fR|\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fB\-\-tool\fR> <\fIkey\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Resolve a stored tool response by the key it carries, with no handle to look up first
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-tool\fR
The tool whose response to resolve, matched whole or as a `__`\-delimited final segment; repeatable
.TP
\fB\-\-key\-at\fR
The dotted path the key sits at in the response
.TP
\fB\-\-raw\fR
Write the selected bytes to stdout verbatim, with no decode and no added newline
.TP
\fB\-J\fR, \fB\-\-json\fR
Emit byte\-stable JSON instead of pointer lines
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIkey\fR>
The key the response must carry, e.g. an issue id
